    "body": "Depends on: cover fineness sweep (decide whether geometry or evidence is the bottleneck first). Cover induction currently runs on the deterministic context-bundle geometry (i64 dyadic bundle). The TeacherOracle trace surface (observe.rs: hidden_state(), top_k()) exists but is unused. Wire it as a second observation lane: run cover induction over final hidden states for a fixed sample, and compare region quality (reference recall, Gate C) against the bundle lane at the same region budget. Acceptance: a per-lane comparison table and a recorded lane choice; the trace surface gains a quantized (i8) spill path per plan §4.1 memory rules if adopted.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- A hidden-state observation lane (TeacherOracle trace surface) exists alongside the bundle lane, and both lanes are evaluated at the same region budget.\n- A lane choice (bundle / hidden-state / union) is recorded with measured evidence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Cover induction runs end-to-end over final hidden states for a fixed observation sample.\n- [ ] Per-lane reference recall and Gate C numbers are compared in one table.\n- [ ] If adopted: quantized (i8) spill for hidden-state vectors per plan §4.1 memory rules, with the memory budget honored.\n- [ ] If rejected: the comparison table showing no gain is attached.",
